<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Barton returns two weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg each morning for a recurrent depressive episode. She took the two weeks of medical leave and has not been to the office, though she admits to answering some messages from home. She had mild nausea and loose stools in the first week, which have settled; she has had no headache, restlessness, agitation, or bleeding. She has missed no doses. She still wakes at 3 or 4 in the morning but now sleeps four to five hours. Her energy and interest are still low, though she walked with a friend twice this week. She has had no suicidal thoughts since the first visit and keeps her safety plan in her bag. Her first cognitive behavioral therapy session is booked for this week. She saw Dr. Mendes of psychiatry this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medication tolerance</td><td>Mild nausea and loose stools in week one, now settled; no agitation or restlessness</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>No missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Four to five hours, with early waking</td></tr><tr><td>Work</td><td>On two weeks of medical leave; answering some messages from home</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts since intake; safety plan carried</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>16, down from 18</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

