    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, recurrent, moderate (F33.1)</content>. PHQ-9 16, down from 18 after two weeks, which is expected this early. Sertraline is well tolerated. Psychiatry confirms a recurrent major depressive episode, with no bipolar, psychotic, or PTSD features. Suicide risk is low, with no ideation since intake and protective factors unchanged. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg; review in four weeks, at six weeks of treatment, and increase to 100 mg if the PHQ-9 has fallen by less than 50 percent, as Dr. Mendes advised.</item><item>Start weekly cognitive behavioral therapy this week.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Occupational burnout (Z73.0)</content>. On medical leave but still answering messages, which keeps work in her head at night. [S]<list><item>A colleague will hold her inbox until her return; phased return from next week at no more than 25 hours a week, with no evening work.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>Baseline, then at least monthly during acute treatment; every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>16, down from 18 at intake (11 percent)</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>SSRI tolerability check two weeks after starting</td><td>2 weeks after starting and after each dose change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Early nausea and loose stools settled; no activation, agitation, or bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9)</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior since intake; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0. Protective factors unchanged. Safety plan reviewed: she carries her copy and has 988 and the clinic number saved</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and adverse-effect review</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no headache, tremor, sexual side effects, or bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Bipolar screen at the initial workup</td><td>Once, at the initial depression workup</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Psychiatric interview today found no past manic or hypomanic episode; no Mood Disorder Questionnaire score is recorded</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Psychiatry consultation</td><td>For recurrent or complex episodes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today; diagnosis confirmed; combination treatment and titration plan agreed</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Psychotherapy, sleep, activity, and social contact</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>CBT starts this week; two walks with a friend; sleep four to five hours</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lithium, anticonvulsant, or antipsychotic monitoring (levels, metabolic tests, AIMS)</td><td>Only on those drugs</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Treated with an SSRI only</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Response (PHQ-9 down by at least 50 percent) by twelve weeks. In progress; target 2026-04-14 [S]</item><item>Remission (PHQ-9 below 5) and continuation treatment for at least twelve months after remission. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item><item>Sleep at least six hours most nights. In progress; target 2026-04-14 [S]</item><item>Phased return to work at no more than 45 hours a week, with no field deployment for at least six months. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item><item>Time with friends or her faith community at least twice a week. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Depression review in four weeks, six weeks after starting sertraline. Next scheduled visit 2026-03-03: six-week depression treatment review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
